  "titleEn": "Rock Band",
  "titleEs": "Grupo de rock",
  "titleText": {
    "es": "Tengo que añadirle algo a la barra para que haga clic como los controladores viejos. Estoy tan acostrumbrado a esa respuesta que el silencio me despista.",
    "en": "I'm gonna have to add something to the strum bar so it makes a clicky sound like the old controllers.  I'm so used to the feedback; the silence throws me off.",
    "noteEn": "The Spanish archive misspells acostumbrado as acostrumbrado. The title text refers to the quieter strum bar on the Rock Band guitar controller and the missing tactile click of older rhythm-game controllers."
  },
  "cardDefinitions": [
    {
      "id": "word-sabéis--you-know-discourse",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "sabéis",
      "answerEn": "you know? (addressing several people informally, mainly in Spain)",
      "noteEn": "Sabéis is the present form of saber used with vosotros or vosotras, the informal plural ‘you’ used mainly in Spain. As a brief question, ¿sabéis? can introduce a remark much like English ‘you know?’ or ‘you know what?’",
      "example": { "es": "¿Sabéis? Tengo una idea.", "en": "You know what? I have an idea." },
      "tags": ["word", "saber", "discourse", "vosotros", "Spain", "A2"]
    },
